{"id":"chatcmpl-35cdeaea-d1c3-4454-9d14-7849c71effba","object":"chat.completion","created":1795249406,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-first visual question answering strategy: first query a domain expert tool to establish presence and laterality, then independently confirm with a grounded localization tool before answering. The key insight is that laterality questions (left vs. right) require explicit spatial grounding because radiological convention flips image-left to patient-right, making naive visual inspection error-prone. Cross-checking two independent tools before committing to an answer reduces laterality mistakes.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"For presence+attribute questions, first ask a domain expert tool an open-ended question to establish what exists, then use a grounding/localization tool to independently verify the specific attribute.\",\n    \"For laterality or spatial-orientation questions, always require an explicit localization step because conventions (e.g., radiological left/right) can invert naive visual interpretation.\",\n    \"Decompose binary-choice medical image questions into (1) presence detection and (2) attribute/side determination, answering only after both are confirmed.\",\n    \"When two independent tools agree on the same finding, commit to the answer; treat tool agreement as the confidence signal rather than single-tool output.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Use an expert-reader tool for the clinical finding, then a grounding tool to confirm location/side; never answer laterality from raw visual inspection alone.\",\n    \"Binary-choice visual questions\": \"Convert the choice into a presence check plus an attribute check, and let the attribute check disambiguate between options.\",\n    \"Tool-augmented reasoning\": \"Chain a semantic/expert tool with a spatial/grounding tool; require convergence before finalizing the answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding is actually present before deciding which side or variant applies.\",\n    \"Verify laterality with an explicit localization/grounding step, accounting for image-vs-patient orientation conventions.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":423,"total_tokens":822,"completion_tokens":399,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":423},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":399}}}